# `core.autocrlf` is true on this bench, but docs/HANDOFF.md was committed with
# CRLF already in the blob. Left alone, every edit to it stages as a whole-file
# rewrite -- 2,700 lines changed to show 60 -- which buries the actual change and
# breaks `git log` as the incident record for the one file that most depends on
# being readable that way.
#
# `-text` tells git to store the bytes as they are, so the existing CRLF blob
# stays and diffs stay small. The alternative, normalising to LF, is a one-time
# whole-file commit; worth doing deliberately some day, not as a side effect of
# an edit.
docs/HANDOFF.md -text
